   "id": "ca_variation_to_the_great_chimney",
   "area_id": "ca_florence_peak",
   "name": "Variation to The Great Chimney",
   "grade": "5.8",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "The route starts on a ledge five feet off the ground, slightly left of the Great Chimney; its alcove shields the belayer. P1 trends up and left about 100' over low 5th class terrain, with occasional 5.8 boulder moves, ending on any convenient ledge. P2 climbs a flake, then a hand traverse leftward gets into a chimney of loose 5.6 rock; at its end, blocks and cracks reach a ledge, and a walk to the right arrives atop the Great Chimney. A class 2 gully, then class 3 ground up and right, leads to a blunt arete that rejoins the standard route. Two easy roped pitches reach the summit ridge. Adventure route: ledges are debris-covered and several big blocks move; keep the belayer protected.",
